WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:03.900
Changes in your diet not
only affect you physically,

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:05.820
physiologically inside,

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:08.580
but also mentally,
how well you think,

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:11.100
psychologically,
how well you feel.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:14.160
But you’ll never know just
how good you can feel

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:19.020
until you put it to the test
and try eating healthy.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:21.300
Welcome to the
NutritionFacts Podcast.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:24.000
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.940
Today we follow a
fascinating case study

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:29.280
on the reversal of
stage 3 cancer

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:31.251
with fasting.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:34.680
After a cancer diagnosis,
the focus is understandably

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:36.960
on monitoring the spread
and resurgence of the cancer,

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:41.040
but patients often also want
to know what additional steps

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:44.220
they themselves can take
to support their body’s fight.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.360
Previously, I addressed what to eat
after a cancer diagnosis.

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:51.240
What about eating
nothing at all?

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:54.120
Fasting is purported
to “ameliorate” cancers,

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:57.000
but to support such claims,
they cite studies like this

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.100
on castrated mice.

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:02.400
That’s because there are no
human studies of efficacy,

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.500
though there are
a few case reports.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:09.600
For example: “Water-only fasting
and an exclusively plant foods diet

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:12.720
in the management
of... follicular lymphoma.”

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:14.580
Traditional chemotherapy has been

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:16.920
the mainstay of treatment
for follicular lymphoma.

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:20.580
But in the majority of patients,
the cancer surges back

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:23.880
within a few years, and the chemo
is associated with immediate

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:27.480
and enduring toxicities,
including secondary malignancies,

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:30.780
meaning new cancers caused
by the chemo drugs themselves,

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:33.720
raising the question
of whether chemotherapy

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:35.700
should be abandoned
for the disease.&nbsp;

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:36.480
&nbsp;
So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:38.820
anyway, a 42-year-old
woman presented

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:40.980
to her primary care provider
with a palpable mass

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:43.980
in her groin and was
immediately sent for a CT scan.

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:46.680
Surgical biopsy
confirmed the diagnosis

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:48.900
of a low-grade
follicular lymphoma.

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:52.500
They then found involvement
in the lymph nodes in her armpit,

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.620
which would make it stage 3,
meaning spread throughout the body.

00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:58.320
Because it didn’t
appear to be aggressive,

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:00.060
she was just
advised to follow-up

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:02.100
every three months
to monitor its spread.

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:04.740
But she didn’t want
to just sit around.

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:07.620
So, she contacted the
TrueNorth Health Center in California

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:11.460
to explore medically
supervised, water-only fasting.

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:15.420
She had never smoked tobacco,
but she had consumed

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:17.820
the Standard American Diet;
so they started her

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:20.880
on a whole food plant
foods diet free

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:22.680
of added salt,
oil, and sugar.

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:28.020
Then, she did 21 days on water only,
before transitioning back to a diet

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:31.620
of minimally processed plant foods,
including fresh, raw fruits

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:33.420
and vegetables, steamed
and baked vegetables,

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:36.060
whole grains and legumes,
and about an ounce a day

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:37.200
of nuts and seeds.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:39.720
Okay, so what happened?

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:43.380
On physical exam, her cancerous
lymph nodes seemed to be shrinking,

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:46.980
and indeed, on CT scan,
her enlarged nodes shrunk

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:50.220
up to 90 percent and no
longer seemed to be active.

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:52.800
Before and after.

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:55.140
What could it have been?

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:59.280
She did lose weight, about 20 pounds,
but follicular lymphoma does not appear

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:00.420
to be associated with obesity,

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:03.780
nor does BMI appear
to affect clinical outcomes.

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:07.560
It’s possible the plant-based
diet alone helped.

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:09.960
Follicular lymphoma is the
second most common type

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:13.020
of non-Hodgkin lymphoma, which itself

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:16.200
is the most common type
of blood cancer in adults.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:19.680
Higher intakes of dietary fiber,
whole grains, and several fruits

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:21.000
and vegetables are
reported to reduce

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:24.960
the risk of non-Hodgkin lymphoma,
whereas animal-derived proteins

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:28.080
and fat in meat
and dairy may increase it.

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:31.320
A dietary pattern high
in meats, fats, and sweets

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:33.660
was associated with three times
the risk of follicular lymphoma,

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:35.760
or just the fat and meat
was associated

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:38.820
with up to a fivefold
higher risk. But why?

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:42.060
The thought that foods
of animal origin may increase

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:45.660
the risk of blood cancers
originated from the frequent finding

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:49.740
of an increased incidence among
people who are occupationally exposed

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:54.660
to animals and meats, like livestock
and poultry farmers, butchers,

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:55.800
and slaughterhouse workers.

00:03:55.800 --> 00:04:00.420
It must be acknowledged that
animal foods are a potential source

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:02.760
of infection by
cancer-causing viruses.

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:05.820
But it may just be the animal protein.

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:08.760
Excessive consumption
of animal protein

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:12.480
may encourage malignant changes through
chronic persistent stimulation.

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:15.000
The thought is that
the continuous exposure

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:18.120
to these foreign proteins may
act like a chronic irritant.

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:20.700
The animal protein theory
is bolstered by the fact

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:23.640
that straight protein—
casein milk protein—

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:25.800
increases the number
of lymphomas in rats,

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:30.240
but that doesn’t mean
the same applies to people.

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:33.420
Maybe it’s the hormones
and antibiotics contained in meat

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:35.760
or just the saturated fat,
which may both impair

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:38.400
the immune system and promote
chronic inflammation,

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:39.900
which may play
a role in lymphoma?

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:43.380
Now, it appears to just
be animal fat consumption;

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:46.500
so, maybe it’s just something
building up in the animal fat?

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:50.100
There may be a link between
exposure to industrial pollutants

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:54.540
and non-Hodgkin lymphoma, and food—
especially meat, milk, and fish—

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:56.280
is the immediate
source of almost

00:04:56.280 --> 00:04:58.980
all dioxins and PCBs in
the general population.

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:02.700
Dioxin-like pollutants
build up in animal fat,

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:05.460
which can then be passed
along to consumers.

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:07.260
Vegetarians may
only be exposed

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:09.960
to about 2 percent
of the dioxin dose

00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:12.060
compared to the general population.

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:15.360
The highest single levels
in the U.S. have been found

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:18.660
in chicken, but thankfully
the contamination levels

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:20.940
are declining in all
meats across the board.

00:05:20.940 --> 00:05:24.120
Furthermore, consumers may
further reduce exposures

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:27.660
to dioxin-like compounds by trimming
fat before and after cooking

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:30.480
and by thoroughly draining
fat from cooked meat.

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:33.465
What about buying organic meat?

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:35.940
When it comes to
carcinogenic contaminants,

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:39.420
the differences between organically
and conventionally produced meats

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:43.560
were surprisingly minimal,
exceeding the maximum limits

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:46.020
regardless of what
kind of meat we buy.

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:48.540
Strikingly, not only
does the consumption

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:52.140
of organically produced meat not
diminish the carcinogenic risk,

00:05:52.140 --> 00:05:55.200
but for some meat,
it appeared even worse.

00:05:55.920 --> 00:06:00.900
What can decrease your exposure
to fat-soluble pesticides is fiber.

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:04.680
And then, our good gut flora
can turn fiber into butyrate,

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:07.320
which is absorbed back
into our body from the colon

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:10.800
and acts as a tumor suppressor,
demonstrated in more than

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:15.480
one hundred published studies,
including protecting against lymphoma.

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:18.720
It also has potent
anti-inflammatory effects.

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:21.180
That may help explain why fruit
and vegetable consumption

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:23.460
has not only been associated
with decreased risk

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:27.720
of developing lymphoma, but also
been linked to improved survival.

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:30.840
Maybe it’s all the antioxidants
in plant foods,

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:33.240
which appear protective when it
comes to follicular lymphoma,

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:36.180
but not necessarily
when in supplement form.

00:06:36.180 --> 00:06:38.700
Vitamin C intake
from foods, for example,

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:41.880
may be protective but not
from supplements.

00:06:42.780 --> 00:06:45.240
So, maybe the reason the risk
of lymphomas and cancers

00:06:45.240 --> 00:06:47.640
of the bone marrow tissues
are significantly lower

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:50.460
in vegetarians
and vegans is not just

00:06:50.460 --> 00:06:52.260
because of what they’re avoiding,

00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:56.400
but all the goodies that
they’re getting more of.

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:58.920
The phytochemicals and antioxidants
in fruits and vegetables

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:02.400
may inhibit tumor progression
via a variety of mechanisms

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:05.580
beyond just the potential
adverse effects of meat.

00:07:05.580 --> 00:07:08.340
So, given the link between fruit
and vegetable intake

00:07:08.340 --> 00:07:11.820
and lymphoma survival, maybe
a lymphoma diagnosis can be

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:16.140
an important ‘teachable’ moment
to improve diet in patients.

00:07:16.140 --> 00:07:19.200
That certainly seemed
to be the case here.

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:24.000
At her six and nine-month follow-up,
she reported strict compliance

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:26.400
with her whole food plant-based
diet, and her lymph nodes

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:28.260
remained unpalpable.

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:31.920
Okay, but this
was published in 2015.

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:37.589
How’s she doing now?
We’ll find out next.

00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:41.820
In 2015, a remarkable case report
was published in which a woman

00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:45.360
with Stage 3 follicular lymphoma
underwent a medically supervised,

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:48.960
21-day water-only fast, after which
her enlarged lymph nodes

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:50.880
were substantially reduced in size.

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:54.600
The patient then remained
on a whole food, plant-based diet,

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:59.160
and at 6- and 9-month follow-up
visits she remained asymptomatic.

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:03.720
In 2018, her 3-year
follow-up was published.

00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:06.960
Remarkably, she appeared
to remain cancer-free,

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:08.940
confirmed by CT and PET scans.

00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:12.480
Her cancer appeared to have been
knocked down and out.

00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:16.020
The initial regression has
persisted for the three years

00:08:16.020 --> 00:08:19.680
with no additional intervention
other than the dietary change.

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:22.800
Could it have just
been a coincidence?

00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:26.700
Sure, but the initial regression
directly coincided

00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:30.900
with the timing of her water-only fast,
suggesting a causal relationship,

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:36.060
and there are biological mechanisms
by which fasting may potentiate

00:08:36.060 --> 00:08:39.540
tumor regression, such as
decreasing levels of IGF-1.

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:44.700
The term "spontaneous regression"
of cancer is a misnomer.

00:08:44.700 --> 00:08:47.520
I mean, obviously there was
something that caused the regression,

00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:49.260
whether or not we know what it is.

00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:52.320
Presumably the immune
system plays a role.

00:08:52.320 --> 00:08:55.620
The fact that you can get
a marked increase in cancer rates

00:08:55.620 --> 00:08:58.980
when you're immunosuppressed
suggests that cancers are popping up

00:08:58.980 --> 00:09:03.360
all the time, but your immune system
is normally able to keep them at bay.

00:09:03.360 --> 00:09:08.220
There was an example, for instance,
of a regression after a transfusion

00:09:08.220 --> 00:09:11.040
of blood from a patient
who had previously sustained

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:14.700
a spontaneous regression.
Or cases of patients

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:19.380
who had been free of metastases
for 15 or 20 years, only to develop

00:09:19.380 --> 00:09:23.400
rapidly fatal metastases after
some type of stress or shock

00:09:23.400 --> 00:09:26.280
that apparently sharply
reduced their resistance.

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:31.320
For most cancers, spontaneous
regression is exceedingly rare,

00:09:31.320 --> 00:09:33.540
but lymphoma is an exception.

00:09:33.540 --> 00:09:36.120
Of 140 cases of nodular lymphoma --

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:38.550
which is what they used
to call follicular lymphoma --

00:09:38.550 --> 00:09:43.440
there were 18 cases of at least partial
and 6 cases of complete regression.

00:09:43.440 --> 00:09:47.400
So like 1 in 25 cases
just go away on their own.

00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:50.160
So when you have
follicular lymphoma cases

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:52.860
in which tumors shrink
after any kind of treatment --

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:55.080
in this case after some
herbal supplement --

00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:57.600
you always have to ask:
is this cause-and-effect

00:09:57.600 --> 00:09:59.220
or just coincidence?

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:04.500
Elevated natural killing activity may
be one of the possible mechanisms

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:08.220
responsible for spontaneous
regression of malignant lymphoma.

00:10:08.220 --> 00:10:11.100
Natural killer cells may be part
of our first line of defense

00:10:11.100 --> 00:10:13.740
against cancer by
destroying tumor cells.

00:10:13.740 --> 00:10:16.140
And if you compare
the natural killer cell activity

00:10:16.140 --> 00:10:20.100
of those with malignant lymphoma
that spontaneously regressed

00:10:20.100 --> 00:10:22.860
versus those whose cancer didn't,
or a control group,

00:10:22.860 --> 00:10:26.940
the spontaneous regression group
does seem to be on the high end.

00:10:26.940 --> 00:10:29.580
How can we increase
natural killer cell activity?

00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:31.380
Exercise can do it,

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:34.260
unless, apparently,
you're eating a high-fat diet.

00:10:34.260 --> 00:10:36.960
Those randomized to undergo
an exercise training program

00:10:36.960 --> 00:10:39.780
on a high-fat diet actually
suffered a decline

00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:41.700
in natural killer cell activity,

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:46.140
suggesting training on a high-fat diet
is detrimental to the immune system.

00:10:46.740 --> 00:10:49.320
Eating lots of contaminated fatty fish

00:10:49.320 --> 00:10:52.260
may also adversely
affect NK cell levels.

00:10:52.260 --> 00:10:55.800
But put people on a low-fat diet,
and you can dramatically increase

00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:59.940
natural killer cell activity within
a matter of months by about 50%,

00:10:59.940 --> 00:11:03.540
suggesting that dietary fat might
increase the formation of cancer

00:11:03.540 --> 00:11:07.620
by depressing the tumor surveillance
capacity of the immune system.

00:11:08.700 --> 00:11:13.140
The bottom line in terms of fasting
is that, at present, long-term fasting

00:11:13.140 --> 00:11:16.560
in cancer treatment is supported
only by some case reports,

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:19.140
so more research is
desperately needed.

00:11:19.140 --> 00:11:22.740
Sadly, there is no
current clinical research

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:25.200
evaluating the effects of water-only
fasting and a whole food,

00:11:25.200 --> 00:11:28.140
plant-based diet on follicular
lymphoma in humans.

00:11:28.140 --> 00:11:31.560
Long-term fasting is
certainly not without risk.

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:35.100
In this case, a guy opted
to try a 60-day fast

00:11:35.100 --> 00:11:37.860
instead of chemotherapy
for non-Hodgkin lymphoma,

00:11:37.860 --> 00:11:42.360
ending up hospitalized
in a coma and respiratory failure

00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:44.820
because of Wernicke encephalopathy,

00:11:44.820 --> 00:11:46.860
a life-threatening
neurological emergency

00:11:46.860 --> 00:11:49.260
caused by thiamine deficiency.

00:11:49.260 --> 00:11:55.380
But starting on a healthier diet
seems like a win-win no-brainer.

00:11:55.380 --> 00:11:58.140
Just putting people on a plant-based,
whole food, you know,

00:11:58.140 --> 00:12:01.500
sugar-oil-salt-free diet,
with or without fasting,

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:06.583
is sometimes sufficient to induce
an intense healing response.

00:12:06.900 --> 00:12:09.540
